+    "lesson": 4,
+    "field": "content_html",
+    "find": "<p>The Mycenaean warrior vase is a large painted krater from the House of the Warrior at Mycenae, dated to around 1200 BC. It shows two rows of soldiers with spears, round shields and crested helmets. As a near-contemporary record of Mycenaean military equipment made just before the palace collapse, it is one of the most important pieces of evidence for Mycenaean warfare.</p>",
