+    "field": "content_html",
+    "find": "<p data-narration-id=\"n6\">Among the most technically extraordinary objects from Grave Circle A are a group of bronze dagger blades inlaid with scenes executed in gold, silver and a black niello compound. One of the finest, known as the dagger blade showing a hunting scene, depicts a lion hunt in full flight. The scene is composed across the length of the blade: lions pursue spotted deer while hunters with spears and tower shields advance from the other end. The scene is created not by engraving alone but by inlaying different metals into channels cut into the bronze: the lions&rsquo; spots are applied in a lighter gold alloy, the hunters&rsquo; shields carry detailed patterns, and the black niello background creates a strong contrast that makes the scene vividly legible.</p>",
+    "replace": "<p data-narration-id=\"n6\">Among the most technically extraordinary objects from Grave Circle A is a bronze dagger blade inlaid with gold, silver and black niello. Known as the Lion Hunt Dagger, it shows four hunters confronting a lion; one hunter has already fallen. The figures were made by inlaying different metals into channels cut into the bronze, creating a striking contrast.</p>",
