+    "lesson": 4,
+    "field": "content_html",
+    "find": "<p data-narration-id=\"n9\">Two other gold objects from Grave Circle A deserve particular attention. The <dfn class=\"term\" data-def=\"A vessel used for pouring libations or drinking in ceremonies, often shaped like an animal&rsquo;s head or a cone, and found in elite Mycenaean and Minoan contexts.\">gold rhyton</dfn> from Grave Circle A, Mycenae, is a drinking or libation vessel hammered from a thin sheet of gold into a conical shape. Its smooth gold surface is undecorated, emphasising the value of the material itself. The rhyton&rsquo;s shape closely parallels Minoan rhytons from Crete, again suggesting Cretan influence on early Mycenaean elite culture.</p>",
+    "replace": "<p data-narration-id=\"n9\">Two other gold objects from Grave Circle A deserve particular attention. The <dfn class=\"term\" data-def=\"A gold lion&rsquo;s-head vessel from Grave Circle A at Mycenae.\">gold rhyton</dfn> from Grave Circle A, Mycenae, is in the form of a lion&rsquo;s head. Its animal form makes it a striking example of Mycenaean metalwork.</p>",
